              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Debbie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "When this was made, I substituted cream of celery soup for the celery tops, and added a delicious flavor. Very creamy. I also added 1/2 cup of cheese. This was very good."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Many reviewers commented that this soup was thin, so I started off by reducing the chicken broth by about 25% knowing I always could add more if needed. But even then, it still was too thin. After blending with my immersion blender, I put it back on the stove over low heat and cooked for another 20 minutes to get a thicker consistency. I adjusted the seasonings to our taste, and garnished with a bit of bacon and a sprinkle of shredded cheddar cheese. Certainly not my favorite potato soup, it was simply OK.",
            "datePublished": "2023-09-22T13:18:01.864Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sruasonid"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy! I used baby red and russet potatoes. Saved out the red potatoes when I pureed the rest and kept some of the smaller red skinned chunks in the soup for the mouthfeel. I added salt and a little more pepper. It was delicious and my 6 year old son loved it too. Served it with a green salad dressed simply with oil and vinegar, and crusty Italian bread for dipping.",
            "datePublished": "2023-10-02T22:49:21.556Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jill"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It came out wonderful...perfect for this cold winter evening. I only thing I changed was omitting the salt because the chicken broth I used had way too much salt in it and I even had to dilute that.",
            "datePublished": "2008-01-07T14:57:53.067Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TINEH"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a tasty soup. It was a bit on the thin side so I added some flour in the blender before pureeing. I also threw in a cup of shredded sharp cheddar cheese, which was good. I like having chunks in my potato soup so next time I think I'll puree only half the soup and maybe throw in some cooked corn and sliced celery too.",
            "datePublished": "2002-12-30T15:34:01.420Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HEXTHECAT"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Nice soup. As was said above, adding a little bit of flour will make creamier. As a novice, I added too much, though, and had to add some water. I wouldn't add more than 1/4 cup of flour to the puree, if that.",
            "datePublished": "2003-10-20T19:14:08.717Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Trish"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy recipe but needed tweaking. Why oh why would u discard carrots and celery tops. Taste color texture is all good in soup. I used thebroth and 1 cup of milk and thickened it with corn starch instead of pureeing the potatoes. It turned out great!",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-20T00:43:26.343Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lucy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really didnt cate for this. Bland and Not creamy. Too much work to puree soup when you can make it creamy from the get go. Who really wants to drag out the food processor for soup if you dont have to.",
            "datePublished": "2021-10-16T16:34:55.110Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "fruitdog"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was not bad. I stuck to the recipe but it didn't have the body I was hoping for. I added in rosemary sprigs and smashed some of the boiled carrot, then simmered for a little bit longer. I also added salt and Velveeta ( I'm normally opposed to both) but it served it's purpose for an ill friend, he liked it! Thank you for sharing!",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-12T20:59:55.287Z"
          },
          {
